-- wra2-s50-esa-entitlement.l4: Welfare Reform Act 2012 (UK) ss 50 to 53, employment and support allowance: conditions of entitlement.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part wra2. Host Act short name: WRA2007 = Welfare Reform Act 2007; ESA = employment and support allowance.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt (a converter script's plain-text rendering; not the official text).
-- s 50 amends WRA2007 s 1 (6A) and gives retrospective effect; s 51 inserts WRA2007 1A (duration of a contributory allowance);
-- s 52 inserts 1B (further entitlement after time-limiting); s 53 inserts 1(3A) (no new claims on the youth condition).
-- Tax years are identified by the calendar year in which they begin (2013 is the tax year 2013-14), so "later" is a number comparison.

§ `s 50 Dual entitlement`

-- src:878 | (1) In section 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 (employment and support allowance), after subsection (6) there is inserted—
-- src:879 | (6A) In subsection (3)(f), in relation to a contributory allowance, the reference to a couple entitled to a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance does not include a couple so entitled by virtue of regulations under paragraph 8A of Schedule 1 to the Jobseekers Act 1995.
@ref s 50(1) WRA2007 1(6A) (src:878-879)
GIVEN `the allowance is a contributory allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the couple is entitled to a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the couple is so entitled by virtue of regulations under paragraph 8A of Schedule 1 to the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(1) WRA2007 1(6A) the couple is within the reference in subsection (3)(f)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the allowance is a contributory allowance`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to a contributory allowance"
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `the couple is entitled to a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance`
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what subsection (3)(f) itself covers is not among the sources
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the reference to a couple entitled to a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance does not include a couple so entitled by virtue of regulations under paragraph 8A of Schedule 1 to the Jobseekers Act 1995"
        IF `the couple is so entitled by virtue of regulations under paragraph 8A of Schedule 1 to the Jobseekers Act 1995`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a couple entitled otherwise than under paragraph 8A is within the reference as subsection (3)(f), not among the sources, states it
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:880 | (2) In a case where—
-- src:881 | (a) an award of an employment and support allowance is made to a person in respect of any period of time before the coming into force of subsection (1), and
-- src:882 | (b) the person was not entitled to an employment and support allowance in relation to that period but would have been had subsection (1) been in force in relation to that period,
-- src:883 | subsection (1) shall be regarded as having been in force in relation to that period.
@ref s 50(2) (src:880-883)
GIVEN `an award was made for a period before subsection (1) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was not entitled for that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would have been entitled had subsection (1) been in force for that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(2) subsection (1) is regarded as having been in force for the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `an award was made for a period before subsection (1) came into force`
           AND `the person was not entitled for that period`
           AND `the person would have been entitled had subsection (1) been in force for that period`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In a case where (a) ... and (b) ..." -- the case is outside the subsection
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 51 WRA2007 1A: duration of a contributory allowance`

-- src:888 | (2) In subsection (1) the “relevant maximum number of days” is—
-- src:889 | (a) 365 days, or
-- src:890 | (b) if the Secretary of State by order specifies a greater number of days, that number of days.
@ref s 51 WRA2007 1A(2) (src:888-890)
GIVEN `the greater number of days an order made by the Secretary of State specifies, if there is such an order` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 51 WRA2007 1A(2) the relevant maximum number of days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the greater number of days an order made by the Secretary of State specifies, if there is such an order`
    -- "(b) if the Secretary of State by order specifies a greater number of days, that number of days"
    WHEN JUST n THEN IF n GREATER THAN 365 THEN n ELSE 365
    -- "(a) 365 days": the Act's own default, when no order specifies a greater number
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 365

-- src:901 | (6) In calculating for the purposes of subsection (1) or (4) the length of the period for which a person is entitled to a contributory allowance, days occurring before the coming into force of this section are to be counted (as well as those occurring afterwards).
@ref s 51 WRA2007 1A(6) (src:901)
GIVEN `the days of entitlement before section 51 came into force` IS A NUMBER
      `the days of entitlement after section 51 came into force` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 51 WRA2007 1A(6) the days of entitlement that are counted before the exclusions in subsection (5)` MEANS
    -- "days occurring before the coming into force of this section are to be counted (as well as those occurring afterwards)"
    `the days of entitlement before section 51 came into force` PLUS `the days of entitlement after section 51 came into force`

-- src:897 | (5) In calculating for the purposes of subsection (1) or (4) the length of the period for which a person is entitled to a contributory allowance, the following are not to be counted—
-- src:898 | (a) days in which the person is a member of the support group,
-- src:899 | (b) days not falling within paragraph (a) in respect of which the person is entitled to the support component referred to in section 2(1)(b), and
-- src:900 | (c) days in the assessment phase, where the days immediately following that phase fall within paragraph (a) or (b).
@ref s 51 WRA2007 1A(5) (src:897-900)
GIVEN `the days of entitlement before the exclusions` IS A NUMBER
      `the days on which the person is a member of the support group` IS A NUMBER
      `the other days on which the person is entitled to the support component` IS A NUMBER
      `the days in the assessment phase where the days immediately following that phase are days in the support group or days of entitlement to the support component` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 51 WRA2007 1A(5) the days that are counted` MEANS
    -- "the following are not to be counted -- (a) days in which the person is a member of the support group, (b) days not falling within paragraph (a) in respect of which the person is entitled to the support component ..., and (c) days in the assessment phase, where the days immediately following that phase fall within paragraph (a) or (b)"
    `the days of entitlement before the exclusions`
        MINUS `the days on which the person is a member of the support group`
        MINUS `the other days on which the person is entitled to the support component`
        MINUS `the days in the assessment phase where the days immediately following that phase are days in the support group or days of entitlement to the support component`

-- src:887 | (1) The period for which a person is entitled to a contributory allowance by virtue of the first and second conditions set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 shall not exceed, in the aggregate, the relevant maximum number of days in any period for which his entitlement is established by reference (under the second condition set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1) to the same two tax years.
@ref s 51 WRA2007 1A(1) (src:887)
GIVEN `the days of entitlement by virtue of the first and second conditions, in the aggregate, for the same two tax years` IS A NUMBER
      `the relevant maximum number of days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51 WRA2007 1A(1) the period of entitlement is within the relevant maximum` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not exceed, in the aggregate, the relevant maximum number of days"
    `the days of entitlement by virtue of the first and second conditions, in the aggregate, for the same two tax years` AT MOST `the relevant maximum number of days`

-- src:891 | (3) The fact that a person's entitlement to a contributory allowance has ceased as a result of subsection (1) does not prevent his being entitled to a further such allowance if—
-- src:892 | (a) he satisfies the first and second conditions set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1, and
-- src:893 | (b) the two tax years by reference to which he satisfies the second condition include at least one year which is later than the second of the two years by reference to which (under the second condition) his previous entitlement was established.
@ref s 51 WRA2007 1A(3) (src:891-893)
GIVEN `the person satisfies the first and second conditions set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the later of the two tax years now relied on for the second condition` IS A NUMBER
      `the second of the two tax years by which the previous entitlement was established` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51 WRA2007 1A(3) subsection (1) does not prevent the person being entitled to a further contributory allowance` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not prevent his being entitled to a further such allowance if (a) he satisfies the first and second conditions ..., and (b) the two tax years ... include at least one year which is later than the second of the two years" -- a failed "if", reading (a) of NOTES
        `the person satisfies the first and second conditions set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1`
    AND `the later of the two tax years now relied on for the second condition` GREATER THAN `the second of the two tax years by which the previous entitlement was established`

-- src:894 | (4) The period for which a person is entitled to a contributory allowance by virtue of the third condition set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 (youth) shall not exceed—
-- src:895 | (a) 365 days, or
-- src:896 | (b) if the Secretary of State by order specifies a greater number of days, that number of days.
@ref s 51 WRA2007 1A(4) (src:894-896)
GIVEN `the days of entitlement by virtue of the third condition (youth)` IS A NUMBER
      `the relevant maximum number of days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51 WRA2007 1A(4) the period of entitlement by virtue of the third condition is within the relevant maximum` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not exceed (a) 365 days, or (b) ... that number of days"
    `the days of entitlement by virtue of the third condition (youth)` AT MOST `the relevant maximum number of days`

§ `s 52 WRA2007 1B: further entitlement after time-limiting`

-- src:912 | (1) Where a person's entitlement to a contributory allowance has ceased as a result of section 1A (1) or (4) but—
-- src:913 | (a) the person has not at any subsequent time ceased to have (or to be treated as having) limited capability for work,
-- src:914 | (b) the person satisfies the basic conditions, and
-- src:915 | (c) the person has (or is treated as having) limited capability for work-related activity,
-- src:916 | the claimant is entitled to an employment and support allowance by virtue of this section.
@ref s 52 WRA2007 1B(1) (src:912-916)
GIVEN `the entitlement to a contributory allowance ceased as a result of section 1A(1) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has not at any subsequent time ceased to have (or to be treated as having) limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person satisfies the basic conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has (or is treated as having) limited capability for work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 52 WRA2007 1B(1) the claimant is entitled to an employment and support allowance by virtue of section 1B` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where ... the claimant is entitled to an employment and support allowance by virtue of this section" -- a failed "where" condition, reading (a) of NOTES; entitlement under another section is not excluded
        `the entitlement to a contributory allowance ceased as a result of section 1A(1) or (4)`
    AND `the person has not at any subsequent time ceased to have (or to be treated as having) limited capability for work`
    AND `the person satisfies the basic conditions`
    AND `the person has (or is treated as having) limited capability for work-related activity`

-- src:917 | (2) An employment and support allowance entitlement to which is based on this section is to be regarded as a contributory allowance for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 52 WRA2007 1B(2) (src:917)
GIVEN `the entitlement is based on section 1B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52 WRA2007 1B(2) the allowance is regarded as a contributory allowance for the purposes of Part 1` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the entitlement is based on section 1B`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what else is a "contributory allowance" is stated in WRA2007 section 1(7), not among the sources
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 53 WRA2007 1(3A): condition relating to youth`

-- src:921 | (3A) After the coming into force of this subsection no claim may be made for an employment and support allowance by virtue of the third condition set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 (youth).
@ref s 53 WRA2007 1(3A) (src:921)
GIVEN `the claim is made by virtue of the third condition set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 (youth)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the claim` IS A DATE
      `the date on which subsection (3A) came into force` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53 WRA2007 1(3A) a claim may be made by virtue of the third condition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the claim is made by virtue of the third condition set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 (youth)`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is of a claim "by virtue of the third condition"
        THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the date on which subsection (3A) came into force`
            WHEN JUST commencement THEN
                BRANCH
                    -- fork F-53-1 (NOTES): a provision is in force from the start of its day, so a claim made on that day is "after the coming into force"
                    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no claim may be made for an employment and support allowance by virtue of the third condition"
                    IF `the date of the claim` AT LEAST commencement
                    THEN JUST FALSE
                    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "After the coming into force of this subsection" -- the claim is earlier
                    OTHERWISE NOTHING
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the day subsection (3A) came into force is fixed by a commencement order that is not among the sources
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
